      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="summary">
          <h2>1. Offloading heavy compute from the UI isolate</h2>
          <p>
            Running full-text indexing, large spreadsheet recalculations, speech recognition, or SIMD media transforms on a Flutter/Dart UI isolate degrades frame pacing, while exposing raw heap pointers over FFI introduces use-after-free, double-free, and undefined behavior when Rust panics unwind across C frames.
          </p>
          <p>
            Meson resolves this by isolating 49 native Rust APIs across 8 workspace crates behind a zero-dependency generational arena pattern open-sourced in <code>ffi-arena-bridge</code>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="ffi">
          <h2>2. Generational FFI arenas (<code>ffi-arena-bridge</code>) &amp; panic shields</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Opaque <code>u64</code> handles instead of raw pointers (<code>abi.rs</code>, <code>engine.rs</code>):</strong> <code>ArenaBridge</code> packs slot index + <code>GenerationId</code> into a 64-bit <code>OpaqueHandle</code>. Stale reads or double-frees fail generation checks and return deterministic error codes instead of corrupting memory.</li>
            <li><strong>Mandatory <code>catch_unwind</code> boundary:</strong> every <code>extern "C"</code> entry point traps Rust panics and translates them into structured error codes.</li>
            <li><strong>Bounded slice views &amp; trigram search (<code>trigram.rs</code>):</strong> <code>SafeSliceView</code> enforces explicit buffer bounds alongside a deterministic trigram catalog verified by <code>tests/integration_ffi.rs</code> and the live C99 <code>cdylib</code> binary <code>tests/c_smoke.c</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="dag">
          <h2>3. Incremental DAG spreadsheet engine (<code>sheets_engine.rs</code>)</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Dependency graph &amp; cycle validation (<code>SheetDag</code>, <code>DependencyGraph</code>, <code>CycleDetector</code>):</strong> models cell references as a directed acyclic graph and rejects circular references via DFS/Tarjan validation before propagation.</li>
            <li><strong>Topological incremental recalculation:</strong> edits re-evaluate only the affected downstream subgraph (<code>FormulaEvaluator</code>) with XLSX export, yielding <em>O(1)</em> amortized updates on independent cells.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="ai">
          <h2>4. Zero-cloud edge AI: SQLite RAG, TF-IDF/SIF &amp; Whisper STT</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Sub-millisecond local retrieval:</strong> <code>LocalRagEngine</code> combines <code>SqliteVectorStore</code>, <code>TfIdfIndex</code>, Smooth Inverse Frequency (SIF) sentence embeddings, phonetic/Levenshtein spellcheck, and domain slang dictionaries with zero cloud API calls.</li>
            <li><strong>Offline voice pipeline:</strong> <code>WhisperWorker</code> (<code>crates/meson_speech_worker</code>) handles local speech-to-text paired with pre-generated TTS caches (<code>generate_tts_cache</code>) during outages.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="native">
          <h2>5. Delta patching (<code>qbsdiff</code>), SIMD &amp; <code>meson_gpui</code></h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Binary delta updates:</strong> <code>meson_updater</code> and <code>meson_patcher</code> apply <code>qbsdiff</code> binary patches to minimize update bandwidth on constrained links.</li>
            <li><strong>SIMD media &amp; Win32 recovery:</strong> <code>meson_media</code> accelerates image resizing with SIMD instructions alongside Win32 input-freeze recovery.</li>
            <li><strong>Pure-Rust GPUI desktop exploration (<code>meson_gpui</code>):</strong> 33 Rust files on GPUI CE (<code>desktop_grid.rs</code>, <code>taskbar.rs</code>, <code>window_layer.rs</code>) validate direct GPU-rendered desktop shells without web runtimes.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="validity">
